      { q: "Should I use mono or color noise?", a: "Monochrome grain looks like classic black-and-white film and is the safer choice for most photos. Color noise adds chroma variation, which can look more like high-ISO digital noise." },
      { q: "Can grain fix banding?", a: "Yes. Adding a small amount of noise is a well-known trick to break up visible banding in smooth gradients, such as skies, because it dithers the harsh steps." },
      { q: "Are my photos uploaded?", a: "No. The image stays on your device and the noise is rendered onto a canvas locally in your browser." },
      { q: "Can I remove the noise afterwards?", a: "Not cleanly from the exported file. Noise is destructive, so keep your original image and re-export if you change your mind." }
